{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795154089748108002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"foldable-gaseous-owl","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"2a6a07365bca42b5d0d27cf4e4118266d3a1a9028f9380d8c98e841b633be00a","event_uuid":"b558d30f-ff26-4b40-955f-c89228266dee","position":{"commit_sha":"b654b98e8133fee5f55a3ad43e8cab762afa2aac","position":"1795154021446724001-b558d30f-ff26-4b40-955f-c89228266dee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"abb19df710b7da30c4df27dee91c30a43fef1d5e2743f3144a38aff4e0eff6df","event_uuid":"36ca6b10-a8d4-4edb-9440-e1ec66839cc7","position":{"commit_sha":"12effca45a7e7c5a106224e2ba336ab20cf4068f","position":"1795154059792729001-36ca6b10-a8d4-4edb-9440-e1ec66839cc7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"d47059826f321a6b11e3c669986b0c8bd0975dc08ea4dd6c3ac6f7fa0d1e51de","event_uuid":"ea578ffb-04a2-4623-b8a1-2380172c9290","position":{"commit_sha":"b0f3aa4cde20d79bfae1f7310f50653eb6d2590c","position":"1795154089748108001-ea578ffb-04a2-4623-b8a1-2380172c9290"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795154021446724001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"36ca6b10-a8d4-4edb-9440-e1ec66839cc7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 41 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nSome cases are product output that should be POSIX-form: the agent `search_files` tool prints `pkg\\alpha.py:2:` (`test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py`, `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`), the compaction intent journal records `<tid>\\x-SNAPSHOT.json` (`test_compact_crash_atomicity.py`), and the code-review prompt error names `.rebar\\prompts\\...` (`test_code_review_project_criteria.py`). Others are test fakes or expectations: the replacement-walker fake reducer splits paths on `/` while the product joins with `os.path.join` (`tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py:33`), the AST-guard tests compare `relative_to` output with `jira_family/` (`test_jira_family_boundary.py`, `test_rich_text_seam.py`), and POSIX container paths pass through `Path` (`test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py::test_autodeploy_mcp_run_new_routes_gate_scratch_to_the_parent_bind`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py` (1)\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py` (5)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_jira_family_boundary.py` (3)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_seam.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_code_review_project_criteria.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py` (5)\n- `tests/unit/test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_repo_root_seam.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_user_data_size_a68c.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py` (1)\n\n## Approach\nEmit repo-relative paths with `as_posix()` at the product boundaries named above (the same rule as commit `f163c9c987f`), and fix the test-side comparisons. Remove each line from `path-separators.args` as it passes.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `path-separators.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `path-separators.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args","reason":"remove each line as its test is fixed"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"7a2d-9166-ce30-4c1d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 41 tests still compare backslash paths with forward-slash expectations","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b558d30f-ff26-4b40-955f-c89228266dee","36ca6b10-a8d4-4edb-9440-e1ec66839cc7","ea578ffb-04a2-4623-b8a1-2380172c9290"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795154089748108002,"uuid":"51c8967b-8a4b-47ca-8158-cc5dad609231"}
